//// rakun-validation — the `both — boundary` module: the constraints the server
//// enforces are the constraints the client mirrors.
////
//// Reached via `from "rakun-validation"`. See `../../../AGENTS.md` §
//// rakun-validation and
//// `specs/1.0.10-beta/03-rakun/14-rakun-validation/README.md`.
////
//// WHY THIS MODULE IS `both` AND EVERY OTHER SERVER MODULE IS `erlang`. The
//// milestone's rule is that three things cross the boundary: the serialized
//// payload, the route table, and the validation constraints — "the server
//// enforces / the client mirrors". The usual way to do that is to ship a
//// constraint description to the client and write a SECOND evaluator in the
//// client's language, which guarantees the two drift. This module does not do
//// that: `#[validated]` emits a plain botopink function whose body is string
//// comparisons, length checks and regex matches — no host cell, no `@External`
//// anything — so ONE source compiles for erlang and commonJS and the two sides
//// run the same predicate. What is serialized is only the constraint table,
//// and only for a consumer that is not botopink.
////
//// ONE NAME NEEDS CARE AT THE IMPORT LINE. `validated` exists TWICE in this
//// workspace: here, where it emits `validate<TypeName>` and
//// `constraintsOf<TypeName>`, and in `modules/rakun/src/config.bp` (front 05),
//// where it is placement-only and emits nothing. An application imports it from
//// `"rakun-validation"` and never from `"rakun"`, and never both — see
//// `src/decorators.bp`, `docs.md` § Validation and `modules/README.md`.
////
//// The `files` ORDER in `botopink.json` is a dependency order a consumer's
//// build reads literally — a module listed before a sibling it imports reds
//// with `unbound variable` inside this module's own source — so this tree and
//// that list stay the same story.
////
//// `report` and `table` are the two files with the fewest imports (`report`
//// has none at all): a client bundle that wants only `constraintsOf<TypeName>`
//// reaches nothing that touches a socket or the filesystem.

pub mod report;
pub mod table;
pub mod messages;
pub mod spi;
pub mod constraints;
pub mod binding;
pub mod boot;
pub mod decorators;
